# apps/web's own Docker build context (docker-compose.apps.yml's `web`
# service: `context: apps/web`) — excludes what the `deps`/`build`/`runtime`
# stages in infra/docker/web/Dockerfile never need, so a `web` image rebuild
# does not drag in the host's own ~646 MB node_modules, coverage output or
# prior Playwright artefacts. Nothing here excludes a file the Dockerfile's
# own COPY instructions read (checked: this feature's Dockerfile builds
# clean with this file in place, see progress/impl_full_docker_compose.md).
node_modules/
.next/
coverage/
test-results/
tests-integration/
e2e/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.git/
